From d84ad02045bd694f981657cbd6ed4089c95dd779 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akshat Singh <automobilehacks@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:21:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: defer probe while the EEPROM's NVMEM provider is
 missing

mt76_eeprom_init() turns every error from mt76_get_of_eeprom() into "not
found", so when the NVMEM provider of the "eeprom" cell hasn't registered
yet, the driver goes on without calibration. The MT7603 then takes the
contents of its efuse instead, which is empty on boards that keep the
calibration in flash, and with those values a Nokia G-140W-C locked up
hard right after loading the MT7592's firmware.

Pass -EPROBE_DEFER on, so the probe waits for the provider, as it does
for the MAC address cell.

Signed-off-by: Akshat Singh <automobilehacks@gmail.com>
---
 eeprom.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/eeprom.c
+++ b/eeprom.c
@@ -548,11 +548,21 @@
 int
 mt76_eeprom_init(struct mt76_dev *dev, int len)
 {
+	int ret;
+
 	dev->eeprom.size = len;
 	dev->eeprom.data = devm_kzalloc(dev->dev, len, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!dev->eeprom.data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	return !mt76_get_of_eeprom(dev, dev->eeprom.data, len);
+	/*
+	 * The calibration's NVMEM provider isn't there yet: wait for it
+	 * instead of bringing the radio up without calibration.
+	 */
+	ret = mt76_get_of_eeprom(dev, dev->eeprom.data, len);
+	if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+		return ret;
+
+	return !ret;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mt76_eeprom_init);
